WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.070 --> 00:00:05.090
So, you’ve seen some strange lights in the
sky.

00:00:05.090 --> 00:00:08.980
Maybe you’ve managed to take some photos
of what looks suspiciously like an alien craft.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:14.719
If you’ve been really good this year, perhaps
you were even invited aboard for dinner, drinks,

00:00:14.719 --> 00:00:16.600
and a romantic anal probing.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:22.130
Either way, it’s probably best to keep it
to yourself, otherwise you might receive a

00:00:22.130 --> 00:00:24.240
visit from the Men in Black.

00:00:24.240 --> 00:00:29.060
These days, when people mention the Men in
Black, we tend to think of the movie franchise

00:00:29.060 --> 00:00:34.300
starring Will Smith and Tommy Lee Jones, or
possibly the comic book upon which the films

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:35.570
were based.

00:00:35.570 --> 00:00:37.480
But where did the idea come from?

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.670
And more importantly, is there any truth to
it?

00:00:40.670 --> 00:00:46.070
Sceptics claim the idea of “Men in Black”
is a form of collective hysteria born out

00:00:46.070 --> 00:00:52.309
of overactive imaginations and an overwhelming
willingness to believe ... and there’s definitely

00:00:52.309 --> 00:00:57.590
a case for this ... but perhaps it’s not
quite as simple as all that.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:01:04.460
You see, the real problem with the whole Men
in Black theory is that it’s full of facts,

00:01:04.460 --> 00:01:10.310
lies, facts that turned out to be lies, lies
that turned out to be facts, and facts that

00:01:10.310 --> 00:01:13.580
turned out to be lies that later turned out
to be facts again.

00:01:13.580 --> 00:01:16.440
It’s all very confusing.

00:01:16.440 --> 00:01:23.010
The legend of the Men in Black starts in June
1947 with a man, a boy, and a dog.

00:01:23.010 --> 00:01:27.890
Marine scavenger Harold Dahl was out in his
boat gathering logs near Washington’s Maury

00:01:27.890 --> 00:01:33.360
Island when he saw six doughnut shaped objects
hovering directly overhead.

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.360
You’d imagine that was probably cause for
some concern, but things soon got worse when

00:01:38.360 --> 00:01:44.240
one of them suddenly fell out of the sky in
a shower of metal debris which injured Dahl’s

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:47.149
son and killed the family dog.

00:01:47.149 --> 00:01:50.229
So much for ‘we come in peace’.

00:01:50.229 --> 00:01:55.500
Luckily, in amongst the chaos and dog-death,
Dahl managed to snap some photos of these

00:01:55.500 --> 00:02:01.470
mysterious objects, and he rushed off to show
the evidence to his supervisor, retired military

00:02:01.470 --> 00:02:03.400
pilot Fred Crisman.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:07.890
Crisman went back to the site with Dahl and
was amazed to see one of the strange flying

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.250
objects with his very own eyes.

00:02:10.250 --> 00:02:15.630
You might be thinking this makes for quite
a compelling sighting - two witnesses, and

00:02:15.630 --> 00:02:18.200
one an ex military man, no less.

00:02:18.200 --> 00:02:23.910
Unfortunately, it’s fair to say Fred Crisman
wasn’t the most reliable of men, as he’d

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:30.630
once written to pulp magazine “Amazing Stories”,
claiming to have fought mysterious evil creatures

00:02:30.630 --> 00:02:34.120
when stuck in a cave in Burma during World
War Two.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:38.980
So, yeah, not exactly the kind of guy you’d
want your sister to marry.

00:02:38.980 --> 00:02:43.680
The morning after the incident, Dahl was visited
by a man in a black suit.

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:49.010
This “Man in Black” dealt with him in
the most horrific and terrifying way imaginable

00:02:49.010 --> 00:02:54.060
... he took him to a local diner .... OK,
that doesn’t sound so bad.

00:02:54.060 --> 00:03:00.530
But the black-suited figure really ruined
the mood when he warned Dahl not to say anything

00:03:00.530 --> 00:03:05.660
about the incident, otherwise ‘bad things’
would happen to him.

00:03:05.660 --> 00:03:10.510
But by that point it was too late, the wheels
were in motion and loads of people already

00:03:10.510 --> 00:03:15.790
knew what Dahl and Crisman claimed to have
seen - even the press were getting involved.

00:03:15.790 --> 00:03:21.480
Years later, after a government investigation,
Dahl admitted the entire thing had been a

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:27.060
hoax ... but then a few years after that,
he recanted his confession and claimed he’d

00:03:27.060 --> 00:03:29.720
been coerced into making it.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:34.900
As we’ll see, this kind of wishy washy behaviour
tends to be a bit of a theme with Men in Black

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:35.900
encounters.

00:03:35.900 --> 00:03:40.360
You’re told something that’s supposedly
“true”, then you’re told it’s a big

00:03:40.360 --> 00:03:43.070
lie, then you’re told that it’s true again.

00:03:43.070 --> 00:03:45.480
It’s kind of like watching the news.

00:03:45.480 --> 00:03:50.970
Dahl’s story was first recounted in Gray
Barker’s 1956 book “They Knew Too Much

00:03:50.970 --> 00:03:52.650
About Flying Saucers”.

00:03:52.650 --> 00:03:58.000
It was also in this book that he related the
story of Albert K. Bender, which introduced

00:03:58.000 --> 00:04:00.390
the Men in Black to a much wider audience.

00:04:00.390 --> 00:04:06.680
Bender, you see, was the founder of the “International
Flying Saucer Bureau”, so he wasn’t exactly

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.590
shy about his interest in little green men.

00:04:09.590 --> 00:04:15.840
In 1955, however, he went a bit too far by
claiming he had a document in his possession

00:04:15.840 --> 00:04:22.210
proving the US Government was involved in
a UFO cover-up ... and before you could say

00:04:22.210 --> 00:04:28.430
“tin foil hat” three Men in Black showed
up on his doorstep looking equal parts suave

00:04:28.430 --> 00:04:33.390
and threatening to tell him not to pursue
the case any further.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:38.490
It clearly worked a treat, too, because Bender
immediately stopped his research, completely

00:04:38.490 --> 00:04:44.480
shut down the bureau, and spent the rest of
his life slowly losing his grip on reality,

00:04:44.480 --> 00:04:52.210
while his previously intelligent, well-researched
writings gradually turned into eccentric ramblings.

00:04:52.210 --> 00:04:58.810
Take his 1962 book “Flying Saucers and the
Three Men”, for example.

00:04:58.810 --> 00:05:03.690
By this point, Bender was claiming the Men
in Black could float a foot off the floor,

00:05:03.690 --> 00:05:09.040
that their eyes lit up like lightbulbs, that
they were monsters from the planet Kazik ... and

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:14.220
a bunch of other things that even George Lucas
would reject for being too far fetched.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:20.030
Since Bender, there have been far too many
MIB encounters to cram into one video, but

00:05:20.030 --> 00:06:51.310
there are a couple of stand-out ones.

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:58.190
In 1964, Jim Templeton was visiting Solway
Firth in Cumbria when he decided to take a

00:06:58.190 --> 00:07:00.610
photograph of his daughter.

00:07:00.610 --> 00:07:06.090
When the film was developed, however, he was
shocked to see a white figure in a “space

00:07:06.090 --> 00:07:09.110
helmet” standing behind her.

00:07:09.110 --> 00:07:15.840
When Kodak verified the film as authentic
the story went public, and soon enough Templeton

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:22.840
was being visited by two gentlemen calling
themselves “Number Nine” and “Number

00:07:22.840 --> 00:07:23.840
Eleven”.

00:07:23.840 --> 00:07:27.510
With names like that, they simply had to be
government agents.

00:07:27.510 --> 00:07:34.550
The numbers demanded to visit the site of
the photo and Jim obliged, but when “Nine”

00:07:34.550 --> 00:07:40.220
and “Eleven” realised he hadn’t actually
seen the so-called spaceman in the flesh - well,

00:07:40.220 --> 00:07:44.460
suit - they got angry and stormed out of the
field.

00:07:44.460 --> 00:07:46.040
Talk about touchy!

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:48.060
Maybe that’s why “Number Ten” didn’t
come along.

00:07:48.060 --> 00:07:50.560
He probably couldn’t deal with the tantrums.

00:07:50.560 --> 00:07:57.290
In 1976, Doctor Herbert Hopkins was working
on a UFO case in Maine when he received a

00:07:57.290 --> 00:08:03.040
mysterious phone-call from someone claiming
to be a fellow UFO researcher.

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:08.150
The stranger invited himself over to Hopkins’
house, but when he arrived he turned out to

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:10.360
have a very unusual appearance.

00:08:10.360 --> 00:08:17.090
He had no hair, no eyebrows, was extremely
pale, and, of course, was wearing the obligatory

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:18.150
black suit.

00:08:18.150 --> 00:08:22.860
Either this guy had fallen asleep while drunk
in a college dormitory, or there was something

00:08:22.860 --> 00:08:25.240
decidedly fishy going on.

00:08:25.240 --> 00:08:30.071
If the man’s hairless face wasn’t enough
to set alarm bells ringing, Hopkins’ dog

00:08:30.071 --> 00:08:33.390
went absolutely mental when the guy came in.

00:08:33.390 --> 00:08:37.640
Now, to be fair, dogs aren’t always right
about people.

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:41.349
If they were, then all postmen would be complete
bastards.

00:08:41.349 --> 00:08:48.390
But as it turned out, Hopkins’ pooch was
right to be weary of this character.

00:08:48.390 --> 00:08:52.830
After questioning him about the UFO case,
the stranger told Hopkins to reach into his

00:08:52.830 --> 00:08:55.400
pocket and take out a coin..

00:08:55.400 --> 00:09:02.080
Hopkins did as he was told, and to his astonishment,
the coin vanished into thin air before his

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.790
very eyes.

00:09:03.790 --> 00:09:06.710
And then things started to turn sinister.

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:11.790
The Man in Black asked if Hopkins had ever
heard of Barney Hill, a famous UFO abductee

00:09:11.790 --> 00:09:14.020
who had recently died.

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:18.710
Hopkins admitted that he had, at which point
the Man in Black came out with this threatening

00:09:18.710 --> 00:09:25.080
little gem: “Barney didn’t have a heart
... just like you no longer have a coin.”

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.080
Subtle.

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:30.360
And, let’s be honest, shit-your-pants terrifying.

00:09:30.360 --> 00:09:35.990
Having dropped this threat-bomb, the Man in
Black gently suggested Hopkins might want

00:09:35.990 --> 00:09:40.790
to think about destroying all his research
material and shutting the hell up for a decade

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:42.190
or two.

00:09:42.190 --> 00:09:45.060
Unsurprisingly, Hopkins obliged.

00:09:45.060 --> 00:09:50.350
Most stories follow this same pattern, with
the Men in Black arriving out of nowhere to

00:09:50.350 --> 00:09:53.330
hush up UFO sightings and research.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:10:00.560
But the real Men in Black may actually be
doing exactly the opposite.

00:10:00.560 --> 00:10:05.589
According to the book “Mirage Men”, and
the documentary of the same name, the vast

00:10:05.589 --> 00:10:11.850
majority of UFO evidence was not created by
lonely individuals who just so happen to get

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:17.140
through more tin foil than the average consumer,
but by the US government.

00:10:17.140 --> 00:10:23.560
And that far from covering up the existence
of aliens, they’ve been doing their best

00:10:23.560 --> 00:10:27.130
to make us believe in them this whole time.

00:10:27.130 --> 00:10:33.790
In 2013, Edward Snowden leaked thousands of
classified documents from the NSA.

00:10:33.790 --> 00:10:38.840
Amongst this mountain of information was a
PowerPoint presentation called “The Art

00:10:38.840 --> 00:10:45.070
of Deception”,containing various images
and diagrams pasted with such enigmatic phrases

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:52.570
as “People make decisions as part of groups,”
and “Swap the real for the false and vice

00:10:52.570 --> 00:10:54.070
versa”.

00:10:54.070 --> 00:10:57.170
Intriguing ... but what did it all mean?

00:10:57.170 --> 00:11:03.000
Mirage Men offers up an explanation in the
form of Richard Doty, who features heavily

00:11:03.000 --> 00:11:04.710
in the documentary.

00:11:04.710 --> 00:11:10.140
Doty was an agent for the “Air Force of
Special Investigations” – or Air Force

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:16.670
OSI – an organisation which many ufologists
believe to be the real Men in Black.

00:11:16.670 --> 00:11:23.180
Doty claimed that he and his colleagues would
feed false information to members of the public

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:28.370
using the kinds of techniques laid out in
the Art of Deception with the sole purpose

00:11:28.370 --> 00:11:33.470
of creating a tingle in the underpants of
any budding ufologists.

00:11:33.470 --> 00:11:38.500
According to Doty, the patter went something
like this: “I’m with the government.

00:11:38.500 --> 00:11:43.350
You cooperate with us, and I’m going to
tell you what we really know about UFOs.”

00:11:43.350 --> 00:11:48.640
You’re probably wondering why the US government
would bother with something so ridiculous,

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:55.770
but the reason is actually kind of ingenious
- to obscure the truth beneath a stack of

00:11:55.770 --> 00:11:56.770
lies.

00:11:56.770 --> 00:12:01.970
This was during the Cold War, and America
was busy testing all sorts of different advanced

00:12:01.970 --> 00:12:07.160
and secret technology - tools of war they
most definitely didn’t want the USSR to

00:12:07.160 --> 00:12:09.450
know anything about.

00:12:09.450 --> 00:12:16.520
By using Air Force OSI agents like Doty to
fan the flames of UFO sightings across the

00:12:16.520 --> 00:12:22.610
country, they made sure any strange objects
glimpsed streaking through the clouds would

00:12:22.610 --> 00:12:29.459
immediately be linked with UFOs and little
green men, not top secret spy planes and communist-seeking

00:12:29.459 --> 00:12:31.050
missiles.

00:12:31.050 --> 00:12:35.210
And by the way, while we’re wading through
this swamp of conspiracy theories and exaggerations,

00:12:35.210 --> 00:12:42.190
I should make it clear that the Air Force
OSI is a completely genuine federal law enforcement

00:12:42.190 --> 00:12:43.190
agency.

00:12:43.190 --> 00:12:49.230
It was set up in 1948 to investigate crimes,
protect secrets, warn of threats, exploit

00:12:49.230 --> 00:12:53.630
intelligence opportunities, and operate in
cyber warfare.

00:12:53.630 --> 00:12:59.170
In fact, after pilot training,the OSI remains
the second-most requested career choice in

00:12:59.170 --> 00:13:01.570
the Air Force for officers.

00:13:01.570 --> 00:13:06.330
This is worth mentioning, and even celebrating,
because in the world of the Men in Black,

00:13:06.330 --> 00:13:09.210
a solid fact is a rare beast.

00:13:09.210 --> 00:13:16.560
Mind you, despite apparently being 100% legit,
Doty does come across as a bit of a dodgy

00:13:16.560 --> 00:13:17.560
geezer.

00:13:17.560 --> 00:13:22.170
Which probably shouldn’t be a surprise considering
he claims his role at the OSI was to spread

00:13:22.170 --> 00:13:27.940
misinformation and basically confuse the crap
of everyone who crossed his path.

00:13:27.940 --> 00:13:34.360
Mark Pilkington, the writer of Mirage Men,
believed that some of what Doty said was true,

00:13:34.360 --> 00:13:38.450
some of it wasn’t, and that some of it was
a version of the truth ... which, let’s

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:43.290
face it, kind of sums up the whole Men in
Black phenomenon in a nutshell.

00:13:43.290 --> 00:13:49.110
To illustrate this point, Doty claims to have
been a part of the “Majestic 12”; a secret

00:13:49.110 --> 00:13:55.649
organisation founded by President Truman to
recover and investigate alien aircraft.

00:13:55.649 --> 00:14:01.399
The small problem being that the Majestic
12 very probably doesn’t exist, and even

00:14:01.399 --> 00:14:05.970
most dyed in the wool ufologists think it
to be a hoax.

00:14:05.970 --> 00:14:10.740
Doty does claim to have been involved in a
case well-known among conspiracy aficionados,

00:14:10.740 --> 00:14:17.070
that of Paul Bennewitz, an electronics entrepreneur
based in New Mexico.

00:14:17.070 --> 00:14:23.910
Bennewitz had built his own UFO-spotting equipment
and, in 1979, he started picking up weird

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:30.440
radio transmissions and spotting bright lights
in the sky near his home which he was convinced

00:14:30.440 --> 00:14:37.010
were of alien origin and absolutely categorically
couldn’t have been caused by anything from

00:14:37.010 --> 00:14:38.030
Earth.

00:14:38.030 --> 00:14:44.610
Oh, I think I forgot to mention - Paul lived
just across the road from Kirtland Air Force

00:14:44.610 --> 00:14:45.610
base.

00:14:45.610 --> 00:14:48.790
But yeah I’m sure that isn’t relevant………….

00:14:48.790 --> 00:14:54.430
Anyway, Doty and his colleagues quickly realised
Paul was seeing things he shouldn’t have

00:14:54.430 --> 00:14:57.150
been - namely classified military technology.

00:14:57.150 --> 00:15:01.970
But instead of asking him to stop, they actively
encouraged it.

00:15:01.970 --> 00:15:08.670
They told him they were interested in his
findings, dumped fake props for him to discover,

00:15:08.670 --> 00:15:14.870
and even gave him software that helped him
decode the “extra-terrestrial” signals

00:15:14.870 --> 00:15:16.900
he was picking up.

00:15:16.900 --> 00:15:22.360
Within a few years, Paul was interpreting
alien languages, spotting crashed UFOs in

00:15:22.360 --> 00:15:27.890
the hills, and even sounding the alert for
a full-scale invasion ... but these activities

00:15:27.890 --> 00:15:34.910
came to an abrupt halt in 1988 when Paul’s
family decided it was best for our planet,

00:15:34.910 --> 00:15:40.170
the alien’s planet, and the universe as
a whole, if they just checked him into a psychiatric

00:15:40.170 --> 00:15:41.620
hospital.

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:45.290
Some stories, however, were too nutty even
for Richard Doty.

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:50.340
For example, he completely denied involvement
in the “Project Serpo” papers ... which

00:15:50.340 --> 00:15:54.890
is probably a good thing, because they shared
a lot of plot points with Stephen Spielberg’s

00:15:54.890 --> 00:15:59.690
“Close Encounters of the Third Kind”,
only with the added bonus of a cultural exchange

00:15:59.690 --> 00:16:03.970
program between human beings and the aliens
of the planet Serpo.

00:16:03.970 --> 00:16:10.399
Speaking of films, many conspiracy theorists
believe Hollywood’s sci-fi output is specifically

00:16:10.399 --> 00:16:17.149
designed to make the truth about aliens look
unbelievable to throw us off the scent, or

00:16:17.149 --> 00:16:23.300
perhaps to subliminally prepare the world
for “first contact”.

00:16:23.300 --> 00:16:27.900
For example, the 1951 film “The Day the
Earth Stood Still” --- featuring the appearance

00:16:27.900 --> 00:16:33.839
on Earth of a peaceful alien called “Klaatu”
-- was thought by some to be the government’s

00:16:33.839 --> 00:16:38.070
way of testing the waters for real alien invaders.

00:16:38.070 --> 00:16:40.070
Farfetched, you say?

00:16:40.070 --> 00:16:46.520
Well, maybe ... but producer Darryl Zanuck
had links to the CIA’s Psychological Strategy

00:16:46.520 --> 00:16:53.270
Board, writer Edmund North was ex-military,
and during the making of the movie, director

00:16:53.270 --> 00:16:59.450
Robert Wise is said to have become a firm
UFO believer after talking to several influential

00:16:59.450 --> 00:17:00.950
figures in Washington.

00:17:00.950 --> 00:17:07.329
And while we’re talking UFOs and Hollywood,
we really need to mention Dan Aykroyd.

00:17:07.329 --> 00:17:13.949
Yes, that Dan Aykroyd: comedy legend, creator
and star of Ghostbusters, member of the first

00:17:13.949 --> 00:17:20.509
ever cast of Saturday Night Live, and oh,
yeah, complete and utter UFO obsessive.

00:17:20.509 --> 00:17:25.269
Aykroyd is basically the David Attenborough
of extra-terrestrial lifeforms.

00:17:25.269 --> 00:17:32.200
He was the celebrity face of the “Mutual
UFO Network”, created the 2005 film “Dan

00:17:32.200 --> 00:17:38.890
Aykroyd: Unplugged on UFOs”, and to this
day still plays an active role in the UFO

00:17:38.890 --> 00:17:39.890
community.

00:17:39.890 --> 00:17:44.270
You probably thought that “Coneheads”
and “My Stepmother is an Alien” were just

00:17:44.270 --> 00:17:51.270
fun comedy movies from the 80s and 90s ... but
to Aykroyd they’re both hard-hitting documentaries.

00:17:51.270 --> 00:17:55.619
And yes, Dan Aykroyd has his own Men in Black
story to tell, too.

00:17:55.619 --> 00:18:02.759
In 2002, he was busy filming a UFO-based TV
show when he stepped outside to take a phone

00:18:02.759 --> 00:18:03.759
call.

00:18:03.759 --> 00:18:04.759
from Britney Spears.

00:18:04.759 --> 00:18:10.380
The fact it was Britney, Bitch, isn’t relevant,
but it’s a nice little fact-nugget all the

00:18:10.380 --> 00:18:11.380
same.

00:18:11.380 --> 00:18:17.269
Anyway, Aykroyd was mid-Britney call when
he noticed a black SUV parked nearby.

00:18:17.269 --> 00:18:24.720
A tall man stepped out, dressed all in black,
and gave him a very dirty look indeed.

00:18:24.720 --> 00:18:29.830
Aykroyd did a double take, but when he looked
back, the car had vanished.

00:18:29.830 --> 00:18:36.230
Two hours later, he was told his show had
been cancelled, and to this day has never

00:18:36.230 --> 00:18:38.250
been given a reason why.

00:18:38.250 --> 00:18:39.250
Coincidence?

00:18:39.250 --> 00:18:40.250
I think….

00:18:40.250 --> 00:18:41.250
nnn-yeah probably.

00:18:41.250 --> 00:18:45.359
But hey, I guess we’ll never know for sure.

00:18:45.359 --> 00:18:51.539
Putting Dan Aykroyd’s vivid imagination
to one side for a moment, the Air Force OSI

00:18:51.539 --> 00:18:56.429
version of the Men in Black has been on the
radar again recently thanks to another celebrity

00:18:56.429 --> 00:19:03.769
ufologist, ex-Blink 182 singer Tom De Longe,
who is now co-founder and Chairman of the

00:19:03.769 --> 00:19:05.340
“To the Stars Academy”.

00:19:05.340 --> 00:19:12.249
In 2017, the academy released two videos to
the New York Times -- “Go fast” and “Gimbal”

00:19:12.249 --> 00:19:16.519
--- both of which featured UFOs that were
recorded by Navy aircraft.

00:19:16.519 --> 00:19:24.379
And to the orgasmic satisfaction of UFO nuts
everywhere, the OSI confirmed the videos were

00:19:24.379 --> 00:19:30.710
genuine and that they had no explanation for
the ‘unidentified aerial phenomena’ they

00:19:30.710 --> 00:19:31.710
showed.

00:19:31.710 --> 00:19:37.610
So, is the Air Force of Special Investigations
unit the truth behind the fiction of the Men

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:38.610
in Black?

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:39.610
Perhaps.

00:19:39.610 --> 00:19:44.429
But it’s fair to say the far more enigmatic
versions we’ve covered today will stick

00:19:44.429 --> 00:19:47.539
around in the public consciousness for a good
while yet.

00:19:47.539 --> 00:19:52.590
After all, the OSI doesn’t have its own
theme song, or action figures, or even an

00:19:52.590 --> 00:19:59.419
animated TV series ... well, not yet, anyway
... but at least we know they definitely exist,

00:19:59.419 --> 00:20:00.580
so that’s something.

00:20:00.580 --> 00:20:01.739
Thanks for…

00:20:01.739 --> 00:20:05.009
Sorry, sorry, I have to take this.

00:20:05.009 --> 00:20:09.169
Hello? Yes, this is Arran speaking.

00:20:09.169 --> 00:20:10.219
Calling from where?

00:20:10.219 --> 00:20:12.039
… Oh, I see...

00:20:12.039 --> 00:20:15.070
I've told them too much?

00:20:15.070 --> 00:20:17.489
I have to... really?

00:20:17.489 --> 00:20:21.119
Well, if there’s no other option.

00:20:21.119 --> 00:20:22.940
I'm sorry everyone.

00:20:22.940 --> 00:20:24.059
It’s out of my hands.

00:20:24.059 --> 00:20:24.559
Memory thing flashes

